OpenSSH for Minkar
===================

openssh/ is OpenSSH portable 10.6p1, unmodified:

  https://cdn.openbsd.org/pub/OpenBSD/OpenSSH/portable/openssh-10.6p1.tar.gz
  sha256 a9dc9565dffe8640f64d863cd29a32bc4a3dbdec0566a7fc44c5d6ee767d5f39
  (signature checked with the OpenSSH release key, 7168 B983 815A 5EEF
  59A4 ADFD 2A3F 414E 7360 60BA)

Its licences are BSD-style, ISC, MIT and public domain (see
openssh/LICENCE); it contains no GPL code. It is built without OpenSSL:
only the internal cryptography is used (Ed25519, Curve25519, ML-KEM,
sntrup761, ChaCha20-Poly1305, AES-CTR, UMAC/HMAC), so host and user keys
are Ed25519.

Our files:

* Makefile - builds libssh.a and the programs with bmake; the source lists
  follow openssh/Makefile.in.
* config.h - produced by openssh/configure, cross-compiling with the
  Minkar toolchain and SDK:

    configure --host=x86_64-apple-darwin19 --prefix=/usr --sysconfdir=/etc/ssh \
      --libexecdir=/usr/libexec --with-privsep-path=/var/empty \
      --with-privsep-user=_sshd --with-pid-dir=/var/run --without-openssl \
      --with-pam --with-zlib=no --with-sandbox=no --disable-strip \
      --without-hardening --disable-security-key --disable-pkcs11

  (CC is the toolchain's clang; CPPFLAGS, CFLAGS and LDFLAGS all carry
  --sysroot=<SDK> -mmacos-version-min=10.15, or the header checks see the
  host's headers.)
  Run it again when updating OpenSSH.
* include/ - the headers configure makes in openbsd-compat/include for
  what the SDK lacks (sys/tree.h, sys/queue.h, glob.h, endian.h, netgroup.h).
* sshd_config, pam.d/sshd - the server configuration and its PAM policy.
* sshd-keygen-wrapper - creates missing host keys, then runs sshd; launchd
  starts it (SystemLibrary/LaunchDaemons/com.openssh.sshd.plist).

Installed: ssh, scp, sftp, ssh-keygen, ssh-add, ssh-agent and ssh-keyscan
in /usr/bin; sshd in /usr/sbin; sshd-session, sshd-auth and sftp-server in
/usr/libexec; the configuration in /etc/ssh. The privilege separation user
is _sshd (uid 75), as on macOS.
